-- title:
--   Finite separable extensions of K(x) are curves over K
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, and let $x \in F$ be transcendental over $K$. Write $K\langle x\rangle$ for the intermediate field `IntermediateField.adjoin K {x}` generated by $x$. Assume $F$ is finite-dimensional over $K\langle x\rangle$ and that the extension $K\langle x\rangle \subseteq F$ is separable. Then `IsCurveOver K F` holds, which packages three assertions. First, principal divisors have degree zero: for every $f \in F$ with $f \neq 0$ there is a divisor $D$ of $F/K$ whose value at each place $v$ is the order $v.\mathrm{ord}\, f$ and whose degree is $0$. Second, for every place $v$ of $F/K$ — that is, every valuation subring of $F$ which contains the image of $K$, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring — the residue field of that valuation subring is a finite-dimensional $K$-module. Third, the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free as an $F$-module and $\operatorname{rank}_F \Omega_{F/K} = 1$.
--
--   This is the arbitrary-characteristic criterion identifying a separably generated function field of transcendence degree one as a curve over its base field, in the sense of the project's `IsCurveOver` package. It is the standard entry point for supplying that package, and is invoked by the divisor-class group and Weil-pairing development built on `IsCurveOver`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_isCurveOver_of_transcendental.lean

